===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|daughtren|pl2qual=archaic}}

# One’s [[female]] [[offspring]].
#: {{syn|en|girl}}
#: {{ux|en|I already have a son, so I would like to have a '''daughter'''.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Leviticus|26|29|column=1|passage=And ye ſhal eate the fleſh of your ſonnes, and the fleſh of your '''daughters''' ſhall ye eate.}}
# A female [[descendant]].
#: {{ant|en|son}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1950|month=October|author=w:C. S. Lewis|title=w:The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe|genre=fiction|text='''Daughter''' of Eve from the far land of Spare Oom where eternal summer reigns around the bright city of War Drobe, how would it be if you came and had tea with me?}}
# A [[daughter language]].
# {{lb|en|physics}} A [[nuclide]] left over from [[radioactive]] [[decay]].
# {{lb|en|syntax|of a [[parse tree]]}} A [[descendant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Daniela Isac; Charles Reiss|title=I-Language: An Introduction to Linguistics as Cognitive Science|edition=2nd|publisher=w:Oxford University Press|isbn=9780199660179|chapter=Chapter 7, Some details of sentence structure|page=163|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=o6EdNNWLqyUC&pg=PA163&lpg=PA163&dq=daughter|text=We have distinguished two types of situations from the point of view of the placement of the obligatory X constituent within the phrase XP: one in which X is a '''daughter''' of XP, and one in which X is not a '''daughter''' of XP, but a '''daughter''' of one of the constituents of XP (in an adjunct configuration).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Yicheng Wu|title=The Interfaces of Chinese Syntax with Semantics and Pragmatics|publisher=w:Taylor & Francis|isbn=9781315280646|chapter=Chapter 2, The dynamics of language processing|page=17|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qCElDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA17&lpg=PA17&dq=daughter|text=Following the conventional pattern, the argument '''daughter''' of a node is assigned the index ''n''0 and placed on the left side, and the functor '''daughter''', the index ''n''1, is placed on the right side.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[female]] [[character]] of a [[creator]].
# {{lb|en|informal|uncommon|sometimes|_|pejorative}} {{non-gloss definition|A familiar address to a female person from an older or otherwise more authoritative person.}}

